# fastly_ngwaf_workspace_signal_rule (Resource)

Manages a Fastly Next-Gen WAF `signal` rule scoped to a single workspace: it
excludes a signal from requests that match its conditions, which is how a
false positive on a known-safe path is suppressed.

A signal rule has exactly one action, and that action only ever excludes a
signal, so `action` takes just the `signal` to exclude.

Rules of other types are managed by their own resources -
`fastly_ngwaf_workspace_request_rule`,
`fastly_ngwaf_workspace_rate_limit_rule`, and
`fastly_ngwaf_workspace_templated_signal_rule`. All four can be read back
together via the `fastly_ngwaf_workspace_rules` data source.

## Example Usage

```terraform
resource "fastly_ngwaf_workspace" "example" {
  name        = "Example Workspace"
  description = "Managed by Terraform"
  mode        = "block"

  attack_signal_thresholds {}
}

resource "fastly_ngwaf_workspace_signal_rule" "exclude_xss_signal" {
  workspace_id = fastly_ngwaf_workspace.example.id
  description  = "Exclude XSS signal to address a false positive"
  enabled      = true

  condition {
    field    = "path"
    operator = "like"
    value    = "/contact-form"
  }

  action {
    signal = "XSS"
  }
}
```

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Import

Next-Gen WAF workspace signal rules are imported using a combination of the
workspace ID and the rule ID, separated by a `/`:

```shell
terraform import fastly_ngwaf_workspace_signal_rule.example WORKSPACE_ID/RULE_ID
```
